---
Confirm the requirement against its implementing files.

## Inspect criterion evidence

Inspect every LLM entry in criterionTests and follow its criteria text.

{{> ../shared/inspect-evidence.md }}

Return pass only when the inspected evidence establishes the criterion.

## Record separate criterion verdicts

<!-- Context: verify/judge.rs records criterion ids and fact hashes independently. A single aggregate verdict cannot stand in for the required per-criterion observations. -->
Record each LLM criterion's verdict separately in record_verdict.criteria, copying its criterion id
and factHash from the package.

When multiple LLM criteria exist, the explicit list is required.

Its top-level verdict is pass only when every listed verdict is pass.

## Keep executable evidence authoritative

A programmatic test's evidence comes from run_tests and cannot be replaced with a model verdict.

## Read-only verification

A verify session edits no source, test, or criteria file.
